// Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/startat-statement-dax
// Construct: START AT with a comma-separated value per ORDER BY column.
// Expect: parse
// Reference: rejects - START AT must supply exactly one value per ORDER BY column (2 expected, 1 given)
// Divergence: START AT value list
// Normalized: written from the documented syntax `[START AT {<value>|<parameter>} [, …]]`; names from the page's examples.
EVALUATE
    'Customer'
ORDER BY
    'Customer'[Country] ASC,
    'Customer'[City] ASC
START AT "Germany", "Berlin"
